% ============================================================================
% heat-transfer.query.adj — a worked recall over the physics heat-transfer library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "how does conduction move
% heat?": it states no physics fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded
% table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the
% `heat_transfer_mode` rows and returns the mechanism + the table's source/
% locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the mechanism
% `light_waves`, recall its mode — radiation). A word that is not one of the
% three modes abstains honestly — the engine never invents a mechanism.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli heat-transfer.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "heat-transfer.adj"

? heat_transfer_mode(conduction, $Mechanism)   % expect direct_contact
? heat_transfer_mode(convection, $Mechanism)   % expect motion_of_gasses_and_liquids
? heat_transfer_mode(radiation, $Mechanism)    % expect light_waves
? heat_transfer_mode($Mode, light_waves)       % reverse bind — expect radiation
? heat_transfer_mode(evaporation, $Mechanism)  % expect abstain — evaporation is a phase change, not one of the three modes of heat transfer
